  "sources": [
    {
      "source": "HOKFIRE",
      "url": "https://www.hokfire.com/",
      "field": "abilities",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "Passive",
          "name": "Hidden Dragon",
          "desc": "The Dragon Souls from his last 2 skill uses grant effects to his Basic Attacks, which deal physical damage to up to two enemies. He gains 1 mark upon using skills, for up to 3 marks. Basic Attacks expend all marks for various effects, striking once per mark."
        },
        {
          "type": "Skill 1",
          "name": "Flaming Palm",
          "desc": "Deals physical damage and true damage. Attaches a Fire Dragon Soul to his sword. Basic Attacks deal more damage when this Soul is attached. Enhanced Basic Attacks will deal both physical damage and true damage."
        },
        {
          "type": "Skill 2",
          "name": "Downpour",
          "desc": "Deals physical damage and recovers Health upon hit. Attaches a Water Dragon Soul to his sword. Basic Attacks restore Health and Mana when this Soul is attached. Enhanced Basic Attacks will deal physical damage and restore Health, but restore less for hits on non-hero units."
        },
        {
          "type": "Skill 3",
          "name": "Riding the Wind",
          "desc": "Gains Movement Speed that diminishes over time, deals physical damage, and knocks back enemies. Attaches a Wind Dragon Soul to his sword. Gains Movement Speed while this Soul is attached, 50% extra if on both swords. Enhanced Basic Attacks will deal physical damage and knock back enemies."
        },
        {
          "type": "Ultimate",
          "name": "Infinite Vastness",
          "desc": "Soars into the sky for up to 4.5s, then dives forward to damage and slow enemies. Landing deals equal damage and applies Dread. Gains Attack Speed and Attack Range. Basic Attacks hit 2 more enemies. Can switch Dragon Souls mid-flight."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "HOKFIRE",
      "url": "https://www.hokfire.com/",
      "field": "guide",
      "content": {
        "pros": [
          "Incredible late-game scaling",
          "Long attack range",
          "Great escape tool with Ultimate"
        ],
        "cons": [
          "Vulnerable to high mobility",
          "Needs items to impact the game",
          "Predictable damage output"
        ],
        "gameplay_tips": "## Early Game\nIn the early game, you want to prioritze farming and last-hitting minions, contesting around neutral objectives, and looking to use your range to poke enemies when they step up to last hit. Play around your cooldowns. If you have Skill 1 and either Skill 2/3 up, you can look to use these on the enemy hero and use Ao'Yin's long-range auto attack to deal a lot of poke damage.\n\n## Teamfights\nYour goal is to stay behind your frontline and watch out for enemy threats. Save your Ultimate Infinity Vastness for when you are about to die so you can reposition to safety. With Ao'Yin's long range, you can look to flash in with your Skills to finish off low-health enemies.\n\n## Tips & Tricks\nHaving 2 of the same soul will increase the effectiveness. For example, 2 Fire souls means your auto attacks will deal more damage\nIf you have mixed souls and want 2 of the same soul, tap the soul you want double of\nYou can change souls whilst in the air with your Ultimate"
      }
    },
    {
      "source": "Kurohiko",
